{title: Sing Praises to Our King}
{subtitle: Psalms 47:6–8}
{key: Eb}
{tempo: 107}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] | [Eb] |
| [Eb] | [Ab] | [Bbsus4] | [Cm7] |
| [Cm7] | [Ab] | [Ab] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Eb]The Most [Bb]High is to be [Cm7]feared,
[Bb/D][Eb]A great [Bb]King over all the [Ab]earth.
[Cm]He sub[Gm]dues peoples under [Ab]us,
[Cm]Nations be[Gm]neath our [Ab]feet.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
He [Bb]chooses our inher[Cm]itance,
[Ab]The pride of Jacob, whom he [Bb]loves.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sing [Eb]praises [Bb]to God, sing praises!
[Cm]Sing praises to [Ab]our King, sing praises!
For [Eb]God is King of [Bb]all the earth,
Sing [Ab]praises with a [Bb]skillful [Eb]song.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
God has ascended [Bb]amid shouts,
The [Cm]LORD amid the blast [Ab]of the horn.
[Eb]Joy fills the air in [Bb]celebration,
The [Ab]trumpet calls the [Bb]faithful on.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sing [Eb]praises to [Bb]God, sing praises!
Sing [Cm]praises to our [Ab]King, sing praises!
For [Eb]God is King of [Bb]all the earth,
Sing [Ab]praises with a [Bb]skillful [Eb]song.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Ab]God reigns [Cm]over the nations,
[Bb]Seated on his holy throne.
The [Ab]nobles of the peo[Cm]ples gather,
[Bb]With the people of the God of Abraham.
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Sing [Eb]praises to [Bb]God, sing praises!
Sing prais[Cm7]es to our King, [Abmaj7]sing praises!
For God [Eb]is King of all [Bb]the earth,
Sing [Ab]praises with a [Bb]skillful [Eb]song.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
The [Ab]shields of the earth [Cm]belong to [Bb]God,
He is high[Ab]ly [Bb]exalt[Eb]ed.
{end_of_verse}
